-- Old Age Security Act, PART III, sections 19 and 20: the allowance for the spouse, common-law partner or former
-- common-law partner of a pensioner, who is 60 to 64, and when payment may be suspended. Piece oa2.
--
-- As in section 11, the facts about one person and one month are a record, each paragraph of the section is a rule
-- over it, and one rule puts them together. A judgment the Act leaves to an official (approved, is satisfied, directs)
-- is a fact the caller states. Dates of the sort "the day on which the application is approved" are an official's
-- act and so are inputs; "has resided in Canada ... prior to the day on which their application is approved" enters
-- as the number of years of residence up to that day.
-- AGE (fork F-AGE-1): "has attained sixty years of age but has not attained sixty-five years of age" is not tied to a
-- day by the text. Subsections 19(5) and 21(8) say the allowance ceases on the expiration of the month in which the
-- person attains 65, and 21(6) that it begins with the month after the month in which the person attains 60, so a
-- month is paid when the person is 60 to 64 on the last day of the month before it.

§ `Part III -- Monthly Allowances`

§§ `Allowance payable, section 19`

DECLARE `s 19(1): Relation to the pensioner` IS ONE OF
    `Spouse`
    `Common-law partner`
    `Former common-law partner`

DECLARE `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month` HAS
    `the relation of the person to the pensioner` IS A `s 19(1): Relation to the pensioner`
    `the person is separated from the pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sole reason for the separation is that one of the partners is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) or paragraph 19(6)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
    `the sole reason for the separation is that the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
    `the day on which the separation commenced` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
    `the aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the application is approved, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `the person was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is legally resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was legally resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a joint application of the pensioner and the person has been made for the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an application described in section 30 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 30 (piece oa1)
    `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) and the person has applied individually` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
    `payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 19(4.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived` IS A DATE
    `no supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner for the month if the pensioner's special qualifying factor were equal to one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner for the month if the pensioner were not precluded from receiving a supplement by subsection 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
    `the person is absent from Canada throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month in which the person left Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person has remained outside Canada since leaving` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: Immigration and Refugee Protection Act (no piece; a plain input)
    `the person was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 19(6)(d) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: Regulations section 22.1 (piece oa3)
    `the person is a common-law partner who was not a spouse immediately before the coming into force of paragraph 19(6)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month in which paragraph 19(6)(e) comes into force` IS A DATE
    `the sentence of imprisonment the person is subject to` IS A MAYBE `Sentence of imprisonment`
    `the first day of the period of incarceration` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the month in which the person is released` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month in which the person dies` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the month in which the person becomes the spouse or common-law partner of another person` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- (1.1) "For the purposes of subsection (1), common-law partners do not become former common-law partners if the sole
-- reason for their separation is that one of the partners is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) or
-- paragraph 19(6)(f)."
-- src:521 | (1.1) For the purposes of subsection (1), common-law partners do not become former common-law partners if the sole reason for their separation is that one of the partners is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) or paragraph 19(6)(f).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(1.1) (src:521)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1.1): the common-law partners have become former common-law partners` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is separated from the pensioner`
    AND NOT facts's `the sole reason for the separation is that one of the partners is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) or paragraph 19(6)(f)`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(1.1) (src:521)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1.1): the common-law partners have not become former common-law partners` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is separated from the pensioner`
    AND facts's `the sole reason for the separation is that one of the partners is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) or paragraph 19(6)(f)`

-- (1)(a) "in the case of a spouse, is not separated from the pensioner, or has separated from the pensioner where the
-- separation commenced after June 30, 1999 and not more than three months before the month in the payment period";
-- (1.2) "a spouse is not considered to be separated from the pensioner if the sole reason for the separation is that
-- the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)". "Not more than three months before the
-- month" is read as: the separation commenced on or after the first day of the month three months before the month
-- (fork F-19-1).
-- src:516 | (a) in the case of a spouse, is not separated from the pensioner, or has separated from the pensioner where the separation commenced after June 30, 1999 and not more than three months before the month in the payment period;
-- src:523 | (1.2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), a spouse is not considered to be separated from the pensioner if the sole reason for the separation is that the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(1)(a), s 19(1.2) (src:516) (src:523)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1)(a): the spouse meets the separation condition` month facts MEANS
        NOT facts's `the person is separated from the pensioner`
    OR  facts's `the sole reason for the separation is that the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)`
    OR  CONSIDER facts's `the day on which the separation commenced`
        WHEN JUST commenced THEN
                commenced GREATER THAN (YearMonthDay 1999 6 30)
            AND commenced AT LEAST `the first day of the month that is` (0 MINUS 3) `months after the month containing` month
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- (1)(a.1) "in the case of a former common-law partner, has separated from the pensioner where the separation
-- commenced after June 30, 1999 and not more than three months before the month in the payment period"
-- src:517 | (a.1) in the case of a former common-law partner, has separated from the pensioner where the separation commenced after June 30, 1999 and not more than three months before the month in the payment period;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(1)(a.1) (src:517)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1)(a.1): the former common-law partner meets the separation condition` month facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is separated from the pensioner`
    AND CONSIDER facts's `the day on which the separation commenced`
        WHEN JUST commenced THEN
                commenced GREATER THAN (YearMonthDay 1999 6 30)
            AND commenced AT LEAST `the first day of the month that is` (0 MINUS 3) `months after the month containing` month
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- (1)(b) "has attained sixty years of age but has not attained sixty-five years of age" (fork F-AGE-1: at the end of
-- the month before the month).
-- src:518 | (b) in the case of a spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner, has attained sixty years of age but has not attained sixty-five years of age; and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(1)(b) (src:518)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1)(b): the person is at least sixty and under sixty-five` month facts MEANS
        age AT LEAST 60
    AND age LESS THAN 65
    WHERE
        age MEANS `the age in complete years on` (`the day that is` (`a limit in days` 1) `before` (`the first day of the month containing` month)) `of a person born on` (facts's `the person's date of birth`)

-- (1)(c) "has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which their application
-- is approved for an aggregate period of at least ten years and, where that aggregate period is less than twenty
-- years, was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which their application is approved."
-- src:519 | (c) in the case of a spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner, has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which their application is approved for an aggregate period of at least ten years and, where that aggregate period is less than twenty years, was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which their application is approved.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(1)(c) (src:519)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1)(c): the person has the required residence in Canada` facts MEANS
    aggregate AT LEAST 10
    AND (   aggregate AT LEAST 20
         OR facts's `the person was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the application is approved`)
    WHERE
        aggregate MEANS facts's `the aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the application is approved, in years`

-- (2) "A person is eligible for an allowance under this section only if (a) on the day preceding the day on which that
-- person's application for an allowance is approved that person is a Canadian citizen or, if not, is legally resident
-- in Canada; or (b) on the day preceding the day that person ceased to reside in Canada that person was a Canadian
-- citizen or, if not, was legally resident in Canada." Legal residence is for the regulations (subsection (3), piece
-- oa3), so it enters as a fact.
-- src:525 | (2) A person is eligible for an allowance under this section only if
-- src:526 | (a) on the day preceding the day on which that person’s application for an allowance is approved that person is a Canadian citizen or, if not, is legally resident in Canada; or
-- src:527 | (b) on the day preceding the day that person ceased to reside in Canada that person was a Canadian citizen or, if not, was legally resident in Canada.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(2) (src:525-527)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(2): the person's residence in Canada is or was legal` facts MEANS
        (   facts's `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is a Canadian citizen`
         OR facts's `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is legally resident in Canada`)
    OR  (   facts's `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen`
         OR facts's `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was legally resident in Canada`)

-- (4) "Subject to subsection (4.1), no allowance may be paid under this section to the spouse or common-law partner of
-- a pensioner in any payment period unless a joint application of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner,
-- or an application described in section 30, has been made for payment of an allowance in respect of that payment
-- period and payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part." (4.01) the spouse of an incarcerated
-- pensioner may apply alone and the application is treated as joint. (4.1) the Minister may waive the requirement for
-- an application.
-- src:531 | (4) Subject to subsection (4.1), no allowance may be paid under this section to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner in any payment period unless a joint application of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner, or an application described in section 30, has been made for payment of an allowance in respect of that payment period and payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(4) (src:531)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(4): the requirement for an application and approval is met for the payment period` facts MEANS
        (   facts's `a joint application of the pensioner and the person has been made for the payment period`
         OR facts's `an application described in section 30 has been made`
         OR facts's `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) and the person has applied individually`
         OR facts's `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 19(4.1)`)
    AND facts's `payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part`

-- src:533 | (4.01) If the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3), their spouse or common-law partner may apply for an allowance individually and, for the purposes of subsection (4), that application shall be considered and dealt with as though it were a joint application of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(4.01) (src:533)
GIVEN `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(4.01): the spouse or common-law partner may apply for an allowance individually` `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` MEANS
    `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)`

-- src:535 | (4.1) The Minister may waive the requirement referred to in subsection (4) for an application for payment of an allowance for any month or months in a payment period if an application for payment of an allowance has been made in respect of any payment period before that payment period.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(4.1) (src:535)
GIVEN `an application for payment of an allowance has been made in respect of a payment period before the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(4.1): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` `an application for payment of an allowance has been made in respect of a payment period before the payment period` MEANS
    `an application for payment of an allowance has been made in respect of a payment period before the payment period`

-- (4.2) "the Minister shall, not later than fifteen days before that subsequent month or the first of those
-- subsequent months, notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing that an application is required"
-- src:537 | (4.2) Where the requirement for an application for any month or months in a payment period has been waived under subsection (4.1) and an application is required for payment of an allowance for any subsequent month or months in that payment period, the Minister shall, not later than fifteen days before that subsequent month or the first of those subsequent months, notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing that an application is required.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(4.2) (src:537)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 19(4.1) for a month or months in the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application is required for payment of an allowance for a subsequent month or months in that payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(4.2): the Minister must notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing that an application is required` `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 19(4.1) for a month or months in the payment period` `an application is required for payment of an allowance for a subsequent month or months in that payment period` MEANS
    `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 19(4.1) for a month or months in the payment period` AND `an application is required for payment of an allowance for a subsequent month or months in that payment period`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(4.2) "not later than fifteen days before" (src:537)
GIVEN `the first of the subsequent months for which an application is required` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 19(4.2): the last day on which the Minister may give the notice` `the first of the subsequent months for which an application is required` MEANS
    `the day that is` (`a limit in days` 15) `before` (`the first day of the month containing` `the first of the subsequent months for which an application is required`)

-- (4.3) "Notwithstanding that the requirement for an application [...] has been waived under subsection (4.1), the
-- Minister may require that an application referred to in subsection (4) be made for payment of an allowance for that
-- month or for any of those months, and in such a case, the Minister shall, not later than fifteen days before that
-- month or the first of those months, notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing that an application is
-- required."
-- src:539 | (4.3) Notwithstanding that the requirement for an application for any month or months has been waived under subsection (4.1), the Minister may require that an application referred to in subsection (4) be made for payment of an allowance for that month or for any of those months, and in such a case, the Minister shall, not later than fifteen days before that month or the first of those months, notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing that an application is required.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(4.3) (src:539)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 19(4.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister requires that an application be made for the month or months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(4.3): the Minister must notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing that an application is required` `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 19(4.1)` `the Minister requires that an application be made for the month or months` MEANS
    `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 19(4.1)` AND `the Minister requires that an application be made for the month or months`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(4.3) "not later than fifteen days before" (src:539)
GIVEN `the first of the months for which the Minister requires an application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 19(4.3): the last day on which the Minister may give the notice` `the first of the months for which the Minister requires an application` MEANS
    `the day that is` (`a limit in days` 15) `before` (`the first day of the month containing` `the first of the months for which the Minister requires an application`)

-- (5) "An allowance under this section ceases to be payable on the expiration of the month in which the spouse,
-- common-law partner or former common-law partner in respect of whom it is paid dies, becomes the spouse or
-- common-law partner of another person, or no longer meets the conditions set out in subsection (1)."
-- The first two are facts about the person. The third is the result of the paragraphs of (1) read for each month,
-- which the rule below does, so the composite does not use a separate month for it (fork F-19-2).
-- src:541 | (5) An allowance under this section ceases to be payable on the expiration of the month in which the spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner in respect of whom it is paid dies, becomes the spouse or common-law partner of another person, or no longer meets the conditions set out in subsection (1).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(5) (src:541)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the month in which the person dies` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month in which the person becomes the spouse or common-law partner of another person` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month in which the person no longer meets the conditions set out in subsection 19(1)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(5): the allowance is still payable for the month` month `the month in which the person dies` `the month in which the person becomes the spouse or common-law partner of another person` `the month in which the person no longer meets the conditions set out in subsection 19(1)` MEANS
        notYet `the month in which the person dies`
    AND notYet `the month in which the person becomes the spouse or common-law partner of another person`
    AND notYet `the month in which the person no longer meets the conditions set out in subsection 19(1)`
    WHERE
        notYet MEANS
            GIVEN when IS A MAYBE DATE
            YIELD CONSIDER when
                  WHEN JUST m THEN `the first day of the month containing` month AT MOST `the first day of the month containing` m
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- (6)(a) "any month that is more than 11 months before the month in which the application is received or is deemed to
-- have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived, as the case may be"
-- src:544 | (a) any month that is more than 11 months before the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived, as the case may be;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6)(a) (src:544)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6)(a): the month is more than eleven months before the month of the application` month facts MEANS
    `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month that is` (0 MINUS 11) `months after the month containing` (facts's `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived`)

-- (6)(b) "any month for which no supplement may be paid to the pensioner"; (6.1) "does not apply to a spouse or
-- common-law partner of a pensioner in respect of a month for which a supplement would be payable to the pensioner if
-- (a) the special qualifying factor of that pensioner for that month were equal to one; or (b) the pensioner were not
-- precluded from receiving a supplement by virtue of the application of subsection 5(3)."
-- src:545 | (b) any month for which no supplement may be paid to the pensioner;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6)(b) (src:545)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6)(b): no supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` facts MEANS
    facts's `no supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month`

-- src:553 | (6.1) Paragraph (6)(b) does not apply to a spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner in respect of a month for which a supplement would be payable to the pensioner if
-- src:554 | (a) the special qualifying factor of that pensioner for that month were equal to one; or
-- src:555 | (b) the pensioner were not precluded from receiving a supplement by virtue of the application of subsection 5(3).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6.1) (src:553-555)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6.1): paragraph 19(6)(b) does not apply` facts MEANS
        facts's `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner for the month if the pensioner's special qualifying factor were equal to one`
    OR  facts's `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner for the month if the pensioner were not precluded from receiving a supplement by subsection 5(3)`

-- (6)(c) "any month throughout which the spouse or common-law partner is absent from Canada, having left Canada
-- either before or after becoming entitled to an allowance under this Part and having remained outside Canada before
-- that month for six consecutive months, exclusive of the month in which he left Canada": the month is at least seven
-- months after the month of leaving (as in 11(7)(c)).
-- src:546 | (c) any month throughout which the spouse or common-law partner is absent from Canada, having left Canada either before or after becoming entitled to an allowance under this Part and having remained outside Canada before that month for six consecutive months, exclusive of the month in which he left Canada;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6)(c) (src:546)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6)(c): the person has been outside Canada for six consecutive months before the month` month facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is absent from Canada throughout the month`
    AND facts's `the person has remained outside Canada since leaving`
    AND CONSIDER facts's `the month in which the person left Canada`
        WHEN JUST left THEN `the number of months from the month containing` left `to the month containing` month AT LEAST 7
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- (6)(d) "any month during which the spouse or common-law partner is a person in respect of whom an undertaking by a
-- sponsor is in effect as provided under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act"; (6.2) "does not apply to a
-- spouse or common-law partner (a) who was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which this
-- paragraph comes into force, whether or not they had applied for it; or (b) if an event as provided by the
-- regulations has occurred."
-- src:547 | (d) any month during which the spouse or common-law partner is a person in respect of whom an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect as provided under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6)(d) (src:547)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6)(d): an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person` facts MEANS
    facts's `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person`

-- src:557 | (6.2) Paragraph (6)(d) does not apply to a spouse or common-law partner
-- src:558 | (a) who was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which this paragraph comes into force, whether or not they had applied for it; or
-- src:559 | (b) if an event as provided by the regulations has occurred.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6.2) (src:557-559)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6.2): paragraph 19(6)(d) does not apply` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 19(6)(d) came into force`
    OR  facts's `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred`

-- (6)(e) "in the case of a common-law partner who was not a spouse immediately before the coming into force of this
-- paragraph [...], notwithstanding subsection 23(2), any month before the month in which this paragraph comes into
-- force". The text gives no date for the coming into force: it is an input.
-- src:548 | (e) in the case of a common-law partner who was not a spouse immediately before the coming into force of this paragraph (“spouse” having in this paragraph the meaning that it had immediately before that coming into force), notwithstanding subsection 23(2), any month before the month in which this paragraph comes into force; or
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6)(e) (src:548)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6)(e): the month is before the month in which the paragraph comes into force for a common-law partner who was not a spouse` month facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is a common-law partner who was not a spouse immediately before the coming into force of paragraph 19(6)(e)`
    AND `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month containing` (facts's `the month in which paragraph 19(6)(e) comes into force`)

-- (6)(f) "any period of incarceration - exclusive of the first month of that period - during which the spouse or
-- common-law partner is subject to a sentence of imprisonment (i) that is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of
-- any Act of Parliament, or (ii) that exceeds 90 days and is to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1)
-- of the Prisons and Reformatories Act, if the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered
-- into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act."
-- src:549 | (f) any period of incarceration — exclusive of the first month of that period — during which the spouse or common-law partner is subject to a sentence of imprisonment
-- src:550 | (i) that is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of any Act of Parliament, or
-- src:551 | (ii) that exceeds 90 days and is to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act, if the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6)(f) sentence (src:549-551)
GIVEN sentence IS A `Sentence of imprisonment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6)(f): the sentence of imprisonment is one described in the paragraph` sentence MEANS
        sentence's `to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament`
    OR (    sentence's `length in days` GREATER THAN 90
        AND sentence's `to be served in a prison as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act`
        AND sentence's `the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`)

-- The months of the period of incarceration, after the first and before the month of release (the month of release
-- is the one in which payment resumes, subsection (6.3)).
-- src:549 | (f) any period of incarceration — exclusive of the first month of that period — during which the spouse or common-law partner is subject to a sentence of imprisonment
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6)(f) (src:549)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6)(f): the month is in a period of incarceration, exclusive of the first month` month facts MEANS
        CONSIDER facts's `the sentence of imprisonment the person is subject to`
        WHEN JUST sentence THEN `s 19(6)(f): the sentence of imprisonment is one described in the paragraph` sentence
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    AND CONSIDER facts's `the first day of the period of incarceration`
        WHEN JUST start THEN `the first day of the month containing` month GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` start
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    AND CONSIDER facts's `the month in which the person is released`
        WHEN JUST released THEN `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month containing` released
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- The month of release (the month in which payment resumes under (6.3)).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6.3) (src:561)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6.3): the month is the month of release` month facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the month in which the person is released`
    WHEN JUST released THEN `the first day of the month containing` month EQUALS `the first day of the month containing` released
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- (6.3) "Payment of an allowance that is suspended by virtue of paragraph (6)(f) shall resume in respect of the month
-- in which the spouse or common-law partner is released but only if they (a) have notified the Minister in writing
-- before or after their release; and (b) continue to be eligible for an allowance."
-- src:561 | (6.3) Payment of an allowance that is suspended by virtue of paragraph (6)(f) shall resume in respect of the month in which the spouse or common-law partner is released but only if they
-- src:562 | (a) have notified the Minister in writing before or after their release; and
-- src:563 | (b) continue to be eligible for an allowance.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6.3) (src:561-563)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
      `the person continues to be eligible for an allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6.3): payment resumes in respect of the month of release` month facts `the person continues to be eligible for an allowance` MEANS
        CONSIDER facts's `the month in which the person is released`
        WHEN JUST released THEN `the first day of the month containing` month EQUALS `the first day of the month containing` released
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    AND facts's `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release`
    AND `the person continues to be eligible for an allowance`

-- The limitations of (6) taken together, with the exceptions of (6.1), (6.2) and the release month of (6.3): "No
-- allowance may be paid under this section to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner pursuant to an
-- application therefor for [...]".
-- src:543 | (6) No allowance may be paid under this section to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner pursuant to an application therefor for
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6) (src:543)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6): a limitation bars payment of an allowance for the month` month facts MEANS
        `s 19(6)(a): the month is more than eleven months before the month of the application` month facts
    OR (`s 19(6)(b): no supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` facts AND NOT `s 19(6.1): paragraph 19(6)(b) does not apply` facts)
    OR `s 19(6)(c): the person has been outside Canada for six consecutive months before the month` month facts
    OR (`s 19(6)(d): an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person` facts AND NOT `s 19(6.2): paragraph 19(6)(d) does not apply` facts)
    OR `s 19(6)(e): the month is before the month in which the paragraph comes into force for a common-law partner who was not a spouse` month facts
    OR `s 19(6)(f): the month is in a period of incarceration, exclusive of the first month` month facts

-- (1) The relation decides which separation paragraph applies: a common-law partner who has not become a former
-- common-law partner (subsection (1.1)) has none.
-- src:515 | 19 (1) Subject to this Act and the regulations, an allowance may be paid to the spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner of a pensioner for a month in a payment period if the spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner, as the case may be,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(1) separation, by relation (src:515)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1): the separation condition for the person's relation to the pensioner is met` month facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the relation of the person to the pensioner`
    WHEN `Spouse` THEN `s 19(1)(a): the spouse meets the separation condition` month facts
    WHEN `Common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Former common-law partner` THEN `s 19(1.1): the common-law partners have not become former common-law partners` facts OR `s 19(1)(a.1): the former common-law partner meets the separation condition` month facts

-- (6.3) in the month of release: payment resumes "but only if they have notified the Minister in writing before or
-- after their release": a person who was held back under (6)(f) and is released in the month is not paid for it unless
-- they have notified the Minister.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(6.3)(a) (src:562)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6.3): the month of release does not hold back payment` month facts MEANS
    NOT (`s 19(6.3): the month is the month of release` month facts AND NOT facts's `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release`)

-- (1) with (1.1), (1.2), (2), (4), (5) and (6): an allowance may be paid under section 19 for the month.
-- src:515 | 19 (1) Subject to this Act and the regulations, an allowance may be paid to the spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner of a pensioner for a month in a payment period if the spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner, as the case may be,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(1) lead-in (src:515)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19: an allowance may be paid to the person for the month` month facts MEANS
        `s 19(1): the separation condition for the person's relation to the pensioner is met` month facts
    AND `s 19(1)(b): the person is at least sixty and under sixty-five` month facts
    AND `s 19(1)(c): the person has the required residence in Canada` facts
    AND `s 19(2): the person's residence in Canada is or was legal` facts
    AND `s 19(4): the requirement for an application and approval is met for the payment period` facts
    AND `s 19(5): the allowance is still payable for the month` month (facts's `the month in which the person dies`) (facts's `the month in which the person becomes the spouse or common-law partner of another person`) NOTHING
    AND NOT `s 19(6): a limitation bars payment of an allowance for the month` month facts
    AND `s 19(6.3): the month of release does not hold back payment` month facts

-- (7) "The amount of the allowance that may be paid under this section to the spouse or common-law partner of a
-- pensioner shall be determined in accordance with subsection 22(3)."
-- src:565 | (7) The amount of the allowance that may be paid under this section to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner shall be determined in accordance with subsection 22(3).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(7) (src:565)
GIVEN `the pension equivalent in respect of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplement equivalent in respect of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the monthly joint income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner in the current payment period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 19(7): the amount of the allowance` `the pension equivalent in respect of the month` `the supplement equivalent in respect of the month` `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month` `the monthly joint income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner in the current payment period` MEANS
    `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` `the pension equivalent in respect of the month` `the supplement equivalent in respect of the month` `the spouse's or common-law partner's special qualifying factor for the month` `the monthly joint income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner in the current payment period`

-- (8) "If an application has been made under subsection (4) for payment of an allowance to a pensioner's spouse or
-- common-law partner in respect of any payment period, the Minister may, after any investigation [...], direct that for
-- the purpose of calculating the allowance, the monthly joint income, as defined in subsection 22(1), be determined
-- without taking into account the pensioner's income for the base calendar year in any case where the Minister is
-- satisfied that the spouse or common-law partner, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the pensioner or
-- the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of
-- them at the time the application was made."
-- src:567 | (8) If an application has been made under subsection (4) for payment of an allowance to a pensioner’s spouse or common-law partner in respect of any payment period, the Minister may, after any investigation of the circumstances that he or she considers necessary, direct that for the purpose of calculating the allowance, the monthly joint income, as defined in subsection 22(1), be determined without taking into account the pensioner’s income for the base calendar year in any case where the Minister is satisfied that the spouse or common-law partner, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the pensioner or the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of them at the time the application was made.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(8) (src:567)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 19(4) for payment of an allowance to the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner in respect of the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the spouse or common-law partner, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the pensioner or the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of them at the time the application was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(8): the Minister may direct that the monthly joint income be determined without the pensioner's income` `an application has been made under subsection 19(4) for payment of an allowance to the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner in respect of the payment period` `the Minister is satisfied that the spouse or common-law partner, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the pensioner or the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of them at the time the application was made` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 19(4) for payment of an allowance to the pensioner's spouse or common-law partner in respect of the payment period` AND `the Minister is satisfied that the spouse or common-law partner, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the pensioner or the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of them at the time the application was made`

-- (9) "A direction made under subsection (8) in respect of a payment period is deemed to be a direction made in respect
-- of every subsequent payment period, but the Minister may [...] cancel the direction."
-- src:569 | (9) A direction made under subsection (8) in respect of a payment period is deemed to be a direction made in respect of every subsequent payment period, but the Minister may, after any investigation of the circumstances that he or she considers necessary, cancel the direction.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 19(9) (src:569)
GIVEN `a month in the payment period` IS A DATE
      `a month in the payment period in respect of which the direction under subsection 19(8) was made (any date if none was made)` IS A DATE
      `a direction has been made under subsection 19(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(9): the direction under subsection 19(8) is in effect for the payment period` `a month in the payment period` `a month in the payment period in respect of which the direction under subsection 19(8) was made (any date if none was made)` `a direction has been made under subsection 19(8)` `the direction has been cancelled` MEANS
        `a direction has been made under subsection 19(8)`
    AND NOT `the direction has been cancelled`
    AND (`the payment period in relation to the month containing` `a month in the payment period`)'s `first day` AT LEAST (`the payment period in relation to the month containing` `a month in the payment period in respect of which the direction under subsection 19(8) was made (any date if none was made)`)'s `first day`

§§ `Failure to comply, section 20`

-- 20 "Payment of an allowance under section 19 or 21 may be suspended if the beneficiary fails to comply with any of
-- the provisions of this Act or the regulations, but payment may be resumed when the beneficiary complies with those
-- provisions."
-- src:571 | 20 Payment of an allowance under section 19 or 21 may be suspended if the beneficiary fails to comply with any of the provisions of this Act or the regulations, but payment may be resumed when the beneficiary complies with those provisions.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 20 suspension (src:571)
GIVEN `the beneficiary fails to comply with a provision of this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20: payment of an allowance may be suspended` `the beneficiary fails to comply with a provision of this Act or the regulations` MEANS
    `the beneficiary fails to comply with a provision of this Act or the regulations`

-- src:571 | 20 Payment of an allowance under section 19 or 21 may be suspended if the beneficiary fails to comply with any of the provisions of this Act or the regulations, but payment may be resumed when the beneficiary complies with those provisions.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 20 resumption (src:571)
GIVEN `payment of the allowance has been suspended under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary complies with the provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20: payment of the allowance may be resumed` `payment of the allowance has been suspended under section 20` `the beneficiary complies with the provisions` MEANS
    `payment of the allowance has been suspended under section 20` AND `the beneficiary complies with the provisions`
